Good Morning! And welcome to my email =F0=9F=98=89 This week we did a bunch=
 of cool
stuff, so let's jump in!

Tuesday (Pday)
Today was a pretty good Pday, lets jump in. Today I got to talk with my
family which was awesome! We played a word game called Boggle together, and
shared some laughs and smiles. I am so grateful for such an awesome family!
After wrapping up the call, Elder Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I headed o=
ff to find some
sort of elbow pads for him so he can practice better with his nunchucks
=F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=81 The first store we looked at didn't have anything =
that would work, but
Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 did manage to find a new pair of earbuds haha. N=
ext we stopped
by a fried chicken shop to get some lunch. It was super tasty, I got some
chicken with grated plum on top =F0=9F=94=A5 I even got a few pickles on th=
e side,
all different kinds. One of them was like a dill pickle I think! I love
dill pickles but I can=E2=80=99t seem to find many in Japan. Anyways it was=
 great!
Next we went Back to the toy store, and I asked if they had a specific card
game in stock, which they did not. The owner was nice enough to look it up
for me, and told me to keep checking in and it might be there soon. In the
meantime I Bought a couple packs of Magic the Gathering cards, nothing was
super good for what I'm trying to make currently, but it's no problem. I
guess besides that it was a pretty uninteresting Pday I guess lol =F0=9F=98=
=82 That
night we did have Eikaiwa, so we prepped a bit beforehand. I ended up
teaching a lot about school and some associated vocabulary; it was pretty
fun talking with Katayama san and Keiko san. They are both in the 50-80 age
range, but are both really good at speaking in English. It's pretty fun
teaching them both! Afterwards I shared a spiritual message about how even
though we are surrounded by millions of people, each of us are special,
loved, and recognized by our Heavenly Father. I felt the spirit as I shared
my testimony.

Wednesday
Today We were able to print off some flyers for the music concert in a
little while, and we passed them out for maybe an hour near the end of the
day. We were hoping to do it earlier but there was like nobody on the
streets. Veeeery hot. We also tried to stop by A less active members house
but it ended up being a completely different members house, her name is
Morimoto=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9=E3=80=82It was pretty surprising having her open=
 the door and seeing her
standing there. She invited us in, and gave us some super fancy herb
enhanced water. I ended up being able to talk with her about some herbs and
stuff and told her about how my grandma had mint leaves in her backyard,
and that it was nostalgic. She also has a ton of Doterra essential oils
that I saw on a shelf and enjoyed talking with her a bit about them, and
how my mom loves them. It was really nice to talk, and she expressed
gratitude for our help with the kids Eikaiwa class last week. She's been
very stressed about it, and didn't really have a say in being in charge of
it from what it sounds like. She said because nobody is forcing her to do
it, she's been thinking to herself about how she feels it's kind of useless
and when she should stop it. She thinks that through our help it can
continue to go well, and she's encouraged! We shared a scripture with her
before we left, and offered to come back and help weed around Her house the
next day! So grateful!

Thursday
Today we attempted for go visit and give a blessing to Koumoto=E5=85=84=E5=
=BC=9F who
suddenly got put in the hospital for dehydration, but when We got there
(Hattori=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7 was with us too) the people at the front desk sa=
id if we aren't
his family we can't visit him. Bummer, but afterwards we were able to drive
and visit an inactive member who's coming to our music night. He was really
nice and even knows some pretty solid English. He might end up coming to
our Eikaiwa again in the future! Later that day we went over to
Morimoto=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9=E2=80=99s house to do some weeding. It's been a =
long time since I've
helped anyone weed, it reminded me of helping in my family's backyard
garden. It was super hot! Morimoto=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 also showed us All of =
the cool herbs
she is growing, she definitely had a handful I recognize. After we finished
weeding (just for the day, she wants us to come back) she gave us a super
pretty salad, which was actually delicious. Like definitely up there with
my mom's Thai Chicken Salad. She also sent us away with two frozen pizzas
and some furugura which was appreciated!! After that we headed straight for
the community center for my Jkaiwa class. This time there was a teacher I'd
never met before, who is about the same age as my parents. There was also a
guy named Sou from Korea, but his Japanese is native level. We essentially
just had a fun conversation about all kinds of random things. Sou mocked
Fujita san (the teacher) about his lack of music knowledge and for enjoying
the sound of his tires and the engine when he drives, it was hilarious =F0=
=9F=98=82
we were even able to talk a bit about missionary life, and I shared how my
best friend Mason is serving in Korea. Both Sou and Fujita san seem to
think we're working pretty hard, it was nice. When we got home we looked
again for frogs, then got ready for bed. I don't know if this was today or
another day, but we were able to play Magic the Gathering again together
one night. Anyways I Had a pretty fast start compared to Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=
=E8=80=81, and
could have won the game a bunch in the beginning but just didn't attack So
that he could still try and do things. Anyways, he ended up destroying
everything that was in play (sending It all to the trash) and immediately
after used a card to play everything that just Got trashed under his
control =F0=9F=98=82 it was insane =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82

Friday
Today was a big day of planning and practicing. We started off the day with
a pretty short Zoom meeting for the Media Team, and had our language study
afterwards. We got lunch at the convenience store by the church, and I ate
a sandwich that randomly tasted like soft tacos. Later we met with
Hattori=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7=E3=80=81Nishioka=E3=81=95=E3=82=93=E3=80=81and Ka=
wai=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F for singing practice. It ended up going on
for like 2 hours because people showed up late but it was good. Ok so when
Kawai=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F first arrived, I'd never met him before. I think he=
's a pretty
inactive member, or maybe busy. Anyways he's sung at Carnegie Hall before,
he's big about singing. OK, so he walks in the door, and Hattori=E4=BC=9A=
=E9=95=B7 busts
out his harmonica, and they perform a song called Santa Lucia, And let me
tell you that Kawai=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F probably has the loudest voice I've e=
ver heard anyone
use singing. It was a crazy experience, some pretty awesome vibrato. He's
also like one of the only people I've met in Japan with a full beard. A
couple hours later we had game night, and we played Uno and spikeball (just
Me and my companion, everyone else was too old so they just enjoyed
watching =F0=9F=98=82). Uno definitely had some funny moments. I have had a=
 few crazy
starting hands the last couple times I've played, I=E2=80=99ll attach a few=
 pics.
At the end I shared a past experience and testimony, which I will do my
best to write here:

When I was a kid, I loved playing soccer. My favorite part to play was the
goalie, mostly because I got to touch the ball with my hands, drop kick it
as far as I could, and didn't have to run around as much =F0=9F=98=86 Anywa=
ys, there
was one day where I was pretty spaced out, and while (I thought) my team
was on the other side of the field I was crouched down, picking dandelions
or eating some grass, when suddenly ai heard some shouting and=E2=80=A6 WHO=
OSH! The
ball Was kicked straight into the goal! I didn=E2=80=99t even see the other=
 team
coming! In our lives we all have different chances or opportunities that
are placed in our path by a loving God. However, if we're Sitting around
eating grass, we aren't going to even recognize the chances before they go
past us! I would like to invite whoever is reading this to look for the
opportunities that might even be right in front of your face; I'm sure that
everyone has different opportunities at different times, but a few good
examples could be attending church, reading the scriptures, daily prayer,
lending your time or hand to someone else in need. I challenge you to look
at things from an eternal perspective! I promise that as you make That
effort you will be happier and have an increase of peace and reassurance
day to day. =F0=9F=98=8A In the name of Jesus Christ, Amen!

Saturday
Today we started off the day by heading to a library to volunteer reading
English books for kids. Really simple picture books, but it was fun. There
was a nice lady there in charge named Oobayashi=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 and she w=
as impressed my
paper airplane making skills lol. I actually came up with a new/modified
design on the spot, it was pretty cool. For reference there were some
numbered stickers on the ground along the main entrance of the library, and
Oobayashi=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 explained they were for marking a paper airplan=
e competition
lol. Anyways she was pretty blown away by the paper airplane I made, and
says gonna use it herself in the competition later today lol. We then
stopped by an art exhibition (while doing our language study) and talked
with a lady who owns an art store that we might be able to help volunteer
at! Super cool! Afterwards we got some super tasty Korean Fried Chicken
(KFC) ?? =F0=9F=98=82 and glanced at some kind of samurai movie that was pl=
aying from
a projector in the store lol. Nakamura=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 seemed to think it=
 was pretty lit.
Later we did A bit of music Practice and kind of fell into a slump of
Facebook finding at the church. We did manage to wrap up the day with a
solid conclusion to our SKK (=E9=80=B1=E9=96=93=E8=A8=88=E7=94=BB=E4=BC=9A)=
, however. One random thing from today
was we went to a drugstore to get some snacks to give to a member, and I've
Noticed one of the cashiers the past few times we've been. He's super tall,
probably in his late 40s or 50s, and I've noticed him getting trained on
how to run the front register. I think it's super cute that this big giant
that's probably older (and definitely much taller) than the other workers
is getting instructed in such a humble situation. He's really nice, and
today he was the one who checked out me and my companion for our snacks.
While I was waiting for my companion, I said a prayer, asking that we'd get
a chance to meet with him outside of his work environment. I hope that we
can run into him sometime! He seems like he could be our Friend!

Sunday
Today after church we had some watermelon, I surprised everyone by eating
the rind along with the rest of the watermelon. I had to tell the members
that it isn't an American thing, but rather that I'm just weird =F0=9F=98=
=82 While we
were eating, I placed a dead cicada on Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s=
 arm and he got so
scared =F0=9F=98=82 I didn't think he'd be bothered because he loves bugs A=
nd animals
and stuff but afterwards he told me the thing that creeps Him out the most
is dead bugs lol =F0=9F=98=82 Later we went to go to the Okada Family's hou=
se and
practiced music with Matsuoka=E3=81=95=E3=82=93, Hattori=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7 =
and Nishioka=E3=81=95=E3=82=93=E3=80=82It was pretty
good, and I only almost fell asleep once =F0=9F=91=8D=F0=9F=98=82 Fun fact =
I thought all of the
Okada family were members but none of them are =F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=
=9F=98=82 Okada=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9/=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 apparently
just attends church because we need someone to play the piano for Sacrament
Meeting, and there's nobody else who can do it. Their Whole family is so
sweet and friendly with the members though, I had just figured they were
part of the Branch =F0=9F=98=86 When we got back to the church we had some =
studies,
and before heading home we put a bunch of flyers in people's mailbox; our
musical event is in less than a week! Really hoping we can get a few more
people to show up! While we were walking back to the church to get our
Bikes, we said hi to an old lady walking with a flashlight. She was holding
a trashbag and trying to figure out where to throw out her garbage, and I
guess she thought we were garbage men because she was asking us all these
questions about it lol. We weren't able to give her any flyer or invitation
which kinda stinks, but I am hoping we can meet her again, she was pretty
friendly!

